      "name": "herrick",
      "created_at": "2025-10-15T13:42:50.374Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Yes, absolutely, ERPNext is open-source software, and you can self-host it on your own server without any licensing fees. You can find the source code on GitHub or use the installation scripts provided by the ERPNext community.</p>\n<p>That said, setting it up and maintaining it can get a bit technical — especially when it comes to updates, security patches, and performance tuning. If you’d prefer a smoother experience, AccuWeb.Cloud offers pre-configured ERPNext cloud hosting. It’s optimized, scalable, and ready to deploy in minutes.</p>\n<p>You’ll get full root access, automated backups, high availability, and 24/7 human + AI support, so you can focus on running your business while the platform handles the infrastructure side.</p>\n<p>It’s a great middle ground between full control and hassle-free management.</p>",
